= Phylogenetics — Technical =

A statistical phylogenetic analysis evaluates a topology T, branch parameters and substitution/model parameters θ against aligned data D, often through likelihood P(D|T,θ) or a posterior P(T,θ|D). Results depend on alignment, model class, taxon sampling, priors where used, and the distinction between gene and species histories.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* phylogenetic tree ≠ directly observed history
* sequence similarity ≠ phylogeny
* gene tree ≠ species tree by identity

== References ==
* Ziheng Yang & Bruce Rannala, “Molecular phylogenetics: principles and practice”, ''Nature Reviews Genetics'' 13 (2012), 303–314.
* NCBI Bookshelf, ''Sequence — Evolution — Function'', phylogenetic foundations.
* modern statistical phylogenetics literature on likelihood, Bayesian inference and model adequacy.
